{"reference":"Genesis 8","book":"Genesis","chapter":8,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A flood comparison","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A Neo-Assyrian tablet copy preserves the Standard Babylonian Epic's account of Uta-napishti surviving a divinely sent flood. The supplied comparison concerns boat construction, preservation of life, birds, landing, and post-flood sacrifice in Genesis 6–9; shared motifs support comparison but do not prove a single line of direct borrowing.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_008_feeea3a45fa04dc62a813b48"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
